{
  "title": "Switch the game export wire format to snake_case",
  "description": "The Python API in `schemas/game_export_types.py` is already snake_case, but the serialized game export still uses camelCase keys on disk through `json_key` metadata and parse/serialize remapping helpers.\n\
\n\
That leaves the export layer carrying two naming systems at once. The current setup works, but it adds translation code, keeps schema-backed dataclasses tied to wire-format aliases, and forces tests and consumers to constantly distinguish between Python attribute names and JSON field names.\n\
\n\
Create a new export schema version that writes snake_case keys in the exported JSON itself, add migrations from older exports, update the website/types/tooling to read the new schema version, and then remove the now-unnecessary JSON key remapping layer from `schemas/game_export_types.py`.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- define the next export schema version with snake_case field names on disk\n\
- add migration code from older export versions to the new wire format\n\
- update generated website types and any export readers that assume camelCase JSON keys\n\
- simplify `schemas/game_export_types.py` by removing field-level JSON key aliases and the associated remapping helpers once the new schema lands\n\
\n\
Relevant files:\n\
- `schemas/game_export_types.py`\n\
- `schemas/game-export-v8.schema.json`\n\
- `schemas/migrations/*.py`\n\
- `scripts/migrate_exports.py`\n\
- `scripts/game_exports.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_export_schema.py`\n\
- `website/src/generated/game-export-v8.ts`\n\
- `doc/export-schema.md`",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
